.TH CRON-QUERY 1 "November 2025" "cron-query 1.2.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cron-query \- query crontab schedules with natural language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cron-query
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIQUERY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cron-query
is a command-line tool that helps users understand when cron jobs will execute by parsing
crontab files and providing natural language descriptions of job schedules. Features include
Unicode-aware output formatting, customizable templates, and cross-platform compatibility.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this help message and exit
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show program version and exit
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " \fIFILE\fR"
Read crontab from FILE instead of default location
.TP
.BR \-\-format " \fIFORMAT\fR"
Output format: list, table, json, csv, or yaml. Default is list
.TP
.BR \-\-source " \fISOURCE\fR"
Crontab source: user, system, or all. Default is user
.TP
.BR \-\-template " \fITEMPLATE\fR"
Custom output template or predefined template name (compact, detailed, summary, verbose)
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-templates
List available predefined templates
.TP
.BR \-\-template\-help
Show template help with available variables
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-pager
Disable pagination
.TP
.BR \-\-page\-size " \fINUMBER\fR"
Number of results per page. Default is 20
.TP
.BR \-\-page " \fINUMBER\fR"
Page number to display. Default is 1
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging and detailed cron parsing information
.SH QUERY EXAMPLES
.SS Basic Queries
.TP
.BR "cron-query 'weekdays'"
Show all jobs that run on weekdays (Monday-Friday)
.TP
.BR "cron-query 'Saturday'"
Show all jobs that run on Saturday
.TP
.BR "cron-query '8 AM'"
Show all jobs that run at 8:00 AM
.TP
.BR "cron-query 'after 5 PM'"
Show all jobs that run after 5:00 PM
.SS Relative Date Queries
.TP
.BR "cron-query 'this Saturday'"
Show all jobs that run on this coming Saturday
.TP
.BR "cron-query 'next Monday'"
Show all jobs that run on next Monday
.TP
.BR "cron-query 'today'"
Show all jobs that run today
.SS Template Usage
.TP
.BR "cron-query 'weekdays' --template compact"
Show weekday jobs in compact format
.TP
.BR "cron-query 'Saturday' --template '{bullet} {expression} {next} {command}'"
Show Saturday jobs with custom template using special characters
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/crontab
System-wide crontab file
.TP
.I /etc/cron.d/*
System cron directory files
.TP
.I /var/spool/cron/*
User crontab files
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRON_QUERY_FORCE_ASCII
If set to 1, force ASCII characters instead of Unicode symbols
.TP
.B CRON_QUERY_FORCE_UNICODE
If set to 1, force Unicode characters even if terminal detection suggests otherwise
.SH TEMPLATE VARIABLES
.TP
Custom templates support the following variables:
.TP
.BR {index}
Job number
.TP
.BR {expression}
Cron expression
.TP
.BR {command}
Command to execute
.TP
.BR {description}
Human-readable schedule description
.TP
.BR {next_run}
Next scheduled run time
.TP
.BR {bullet}
Bullet point character (• or *)
.TP
.BR {error}
Error symbol character (❌ or X)
.TP
.BR {next}
Next arrow character (→ or ->)
.TP
.BR {prev}
Previous arrow character (← or <-)
